{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (DOCTOR): Come on in and sit down. This computer's after freezing, so I might ask you things twice.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0003] person_1 (DOCTOR): It's the dizziness brought you in?",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0005] person_1 (DOCTOR): Your daughter rang the surgery. She says you went down twice.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (PATIENT): Slid.",
  "[SEG0007] person_1 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again?",
  "[SEG0008] person_2 (PATIENT): Slid twice. Not fell.",
  "[SEG0009] person_1 (DOCTOR): You slid down. Not what you'd call a fall. Still the twice?",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (PATIENT): Twice.",
  "[SEG0011] person_1 (DOCTOR): When, about? Hang on, wrong tab. When was it?",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (PATIENT): Fortnight.",
  "[SEG0013] person_1 (DOCTOR): In the last fortnight. Did you black out at all?",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0015] person_1 (DOCTOR): Any bang to the head?",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0017] person_1 (DOCTOR): And these dizzy spells. Is it when you stand up?",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0019] person_1 (DOCTOR): Up off the chair?",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (PATIENT): Chair.",
  "[SEG0021] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long has that been going on? The cursor jumped. Say it again.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (PATIENT): Three weeks.",
  "[SEG0023] person_1 (DOCTOR): Three weeks. Any pain in the chest with it?",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0025] person_1 (DOCTOR): Short of breath?",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0027] person_1 (DOCTOR): Heart thumping, palpitations?",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (PATIENT): No.",
  "[SEG0029] person_1 (DOCTOR): Right. The tablets. You're on a few for the blood pressure.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0031] person_1 (DOCTOR): Amlodipine. Is the dose five or ten? I can't read it on here.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (PATIENT): Ten.",
  "[SEG0033] person_1 (DOCTOR): Amlodipine ten milligrams in the morning. Ramipril five milligrams once a day?",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (PATIENT): Five.",
  "[SEG0035] person_1 (DOCTOR): Bendroflumethiazide two point five milligrams, once a day?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0037] person_1 (DOCTOR): Do you take all three every day?",
  "[SEG0038] person_2 (PATIENT): Mostly.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (DOCTOR): Which one do you miss?",
  "[SEG0040] person_2 (PATIENT): Water one. Sometimes.",
  "[SEG0041] person_1 (DOCTOR): And a sleeping tablet. Is it zopiclone?",
  "[SEG0042] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0043] person_1 (DOCTOR): What strength? Two boxes on the repeat and the screen's flickering. Say it again.",
  "[SEG0044] person_2 (PATIENT): Seven point five.",
  "[SEG0045] person_1 (DOCTOR): Zopiclone seven point five milligrams at night. Every night?",
  "[SEG0046] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0047] person_1 (DOCTOR): How long have you been on it? Ah, never mind, that page isn't loading. Any other tablets, vitamins from the chemist?",
  "[SEG0048] person_2 (PATIENT): Biotin.",
  "[SEG0049] person_1 (DOCTOR): Is the biotin yours?",
  "[SEG0050] person_2 (PATIENT): Sister's. Not mine.",
  "[SEG0051] person_1 (DOCTOR): Your sister's. We'll leave that off your list. The nurse took lying and standing pressures. Lying, you were one hundred and fifty-two over eighty-eight, pulse seventy-six.",
  "[SEG0052] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0053] person_1 (DOCTOR): Standing, one hundred and eighteen over seventy-two, and the pulse was eighty-four. Did you go dizzy when she stood you up?",
  "[SEG0054] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah.",
  "[SEG0055] person_1 (DOCTOR): I'd say your blood pressure is dropping when you stand. Postural hypotension, with the three pressure tablets. I'm cutting the amlodipine from ten milligrams down to five in the morning. Leave the ramipril and the water tablet as they are. The zopiclone can stay for now.",
  "[SEG0056] person_2 (PATIENT): Grand.",
  "[SEG0057] person_1 (DOCTOR): Get up slow out of the chair and hold the arm of it. I'll see you back in a fortnight to recheck the standing pressure. If you go down hard, or the dizziness gets worse, ring the surgery.",
  "[SEG0058] person_2 (PATIENT): Yeah."
 ],
